From: Tyler Baker <tyler@baker.engineering>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: gadget: recover ep0 state on stray SETUPEND
Upstream-Status: Pending

When the host issues a new SETUP packet while ep0 is in a control-transfer
stage other than TX or RX (typically STAGE_ACKWAIT, STAGE_STATUSIN, or
STAGE_STATUSOUT), the MUSB controller raises SETUPEND. The existing handler
only transitions TX -> STATUSOUT and RX -> STATUSIN; every other stage just
logs an error and leaves ep0_state untouched, so the main per-stage switch
that follows never reaches the `setup:` label and the new SETUP's RXPKTRDY
is never consumed.

This is a defense-in-depth fix. The primary reproducer on this layer fork
was a FunctionFS daemon that blocked in write(ep1) and stopped reading
ep0 events, which left SET_IDLE's status phase pending; Windows would
then send GET_DESCRIPTOR(HID Report) before SET_IDLE completed and the
controller raised SETUPEND. The daemon side has since been fixed
(dedicated ep1 writer thread, so ep0 reads are never starved), but
ACKWAIT can still legitimately happen and recovering it cleanly keeps the
gadget responsive instead of needing a full re-enumeration.

Reset ep0_state to STAGE_IDLE in the default case so the subsequent
per-stage switch reaches `setup:` and processes the pending RXPKTRDY.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler@baker.engineering>
---
 drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget_ep0.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget_ep0.c b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget_ep0.c
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget_ep0.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget_ep0.c
@@ -683,8 +683,9 @@ irqreturn_t musb_g_ep0_irq(struct musb *musb)
 			musb->ep0_state = MUSB_EP0_STAGE_STATUSIN;
 			break;
 		default:
-			ERR("SetupEnd came in a wrong ep0stage %s\n",
+			ERR("SetupEnd came in a wrong ep0stage %s, recovering\n",
 			    decode_ep0stage(musb->ep0_state));
+			musb->ep0_state = MUSB_EP0_STAGE_IDLE;
 		}
 		csr = musb_readw(regs, MUSB_CSR0);
 		/* NOTE:  request may need completion */
